Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Identifying gene-specific parameters for \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]c\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] (",
 StyleBox["TwoComponentC, TwoComponentCAlt, IdealizedCFit",
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0]],
 ")"
}], "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9650303056072493`*^9, 3.9650303281462708`*^9}, {
  3.967416096527151*^9, 3.967416096954946*^9}, {3.984324862747696*^9, 
  3.984324873628829*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"293bbc4d-ad52-4af4-8d19-\
3b0b01f28a17"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This starts with a matpac, and chooses best fit values of \[Eta] and \
\[Theta] for fitting c, according to the formula c=",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox["\[Eta]", "\[Mu]"], "+", " ", "\[Theta]"}]]],
  CellChangeTimes->{{3.965029023001381*^9, 3.965029025781538*^9}, 
    3.965029064910729*^9, 3.965029099694047*^9, 3.9650292662525473`*^9, {
    3.965029439805159*^9, 3.9650294405415707`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->
  "bb24c15f-4e2f-4dd3-a219-92427a013083"],
 " where \[Mu] is the mean expression of a gene.  The argument \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]samplegoal\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] allows one to \
choose how many genes to use in doing the fit; it is important because the \
length of time to do with fit with tens of thousands of genes can be very \
long, and is unnecessary, as a smaller sample will usually do just fine (e.g. \
1000 genes).  The genes are sampled in a manner the seeks to sample across \
the range of gene expression Log-equally.  The logged gene expression values \
are binned into equal sized bins of width 0.5, and the code samples an equal \
number from each bin, taking the whole bin if there are not enough members in \
it.  It then cuts down the matrix and ematrix to include just those genes, \
and proceeds to find a c-value for each gene.  Then it fits the c-values, in \
Log-space, to \[Eta] and \[Theta].  It produces a graph for examination.  \n\n\
Note that, in future, we may want to add a possibility of cutting out extreme \
c-values from each bin.  "
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965030365306448*^9, 
  3.965030737133586*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6c82d06e-9687-4035-97c8-\
bf0a220f36a7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"TwoComponentC", "[", 
   RowBox[{"matpac_", ",", " ", "samplegoal_"}], "]"}], ":=", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
     "mat", ",", "depthlist", ",", "n", ",", "genetotals", ",", " ", "bl", 
      ",", "genesample", ",", "newmat", ",", " ", "newgenetotals", ",", " ", 
      "newematrix", ",", " ", "fittedcvalues", ",", " ", "params"}], "}"}], 
    ",", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"mat", "=", 
      RowBox[{"matpac", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"depthlist", " ", "=", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"Total", "/@", 
        RowBox[{"N", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", "mat", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
       RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "mat", "]"}], "]"}]]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"genetotals", "=", 
      RowBox[{"Total", "/@", "mat"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"n", "=", 
      RowBox[{"Width", "[", "mat", "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"bl", "=", 
      RowBox[{"BinLists", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Log", "@", "genetotals"}], "->", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Length", "[", "genetotals", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
        "0.5"}], " ", "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"genesample", "=", 
      RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"RandomSample", "[", 
          RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Ceiling", "[", 
              RowBox[{"samplegoal", "/", 
               RowBox[{"Length", "[", "bl", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
         "&"}], "/@", "bl"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"newmat", "=", 
      RowBox[{"mat", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "genesample", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     
     RowBox[{"newgenetotals", "=", 
      RowBox[{"genetotals", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "genesample", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     
     RowBox[{"newematrix", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
       RowBox[{"newgenetotals", ",", " ", "depthlist"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"fittedcvalues", "=", 
      RowBox[{"Quiet", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"c", "/.", 
          RowBox[{"Check", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"FindRoot", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                FractionBox["1", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"-", "1"}], "+", "n"}]], "#"}], "==", "1"}], ",", 
              " ", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"c", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Method", "->", " ", "\"\<Secant\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"c", "->", " ", "\"\<err\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "&"}], "/@", 
        RowBox[{"Total", "/@", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          FractionBox[
           SuperscriptBox[
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"newmat", "-", "newematrix"}], ")"}], "2"], 
           RowBox[{"newematrix", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"1", "+", 
              RowBox[{
               SuperscriptBox["c", 
                RowBox[{"2", " "}]], "newematrix"}]}], ")"}]}]], ")"}]}]}], 
       "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"params", "=", 
      RowBox[{"FindFit", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Log", "[", 
              FractionBox["newgenetotals", "n"], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Log", "[", "fittedcvalues", "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"RealValuedNumberQ", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Last", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Log", "[", 
           SqrtBox[
            RowBox[{
             FractionBox["\[Eta]", 
              RowBox[{"E", "^", "x"}]], "+", " ", "\[Theta]"}]], "]"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ">", "0"}], "&&", 
           RowBox[{"\[Eta]", ">", "0"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Eta]", ",", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "x"}], 
       "]"}]}], ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     RowBox[{"Print", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Show", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ListLogLogPlot", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              FractionBox["newgenetotals", "n"], ",", " ", "fittedcvalues"}], 
             "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"RealValuedNumberQ", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Last", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
        ",", 
        RowBox[{"LogLogPlot", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           SqrtBox[
            RowBox[{
             FractionBox["\[Eta]", "x"], "+", " ", "\[Theta]"}]], "/.", 
           "params"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "0.002", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"PlotStyle", "->", " ", "Red"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
     ";", "\[IndentingNewLine]", "params"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.965029474711892*^9, 3.965029724114294*^9}, {
   3.965029767588723*^9, 3.965029811128416*^9}, {3.965029861062038*^9, 
   3.965029908779766*^9}, {3.9650299759592876`*^9, 3.965030001056531*^9}, {
   3.9650300323910427`*^9, 3.965030050047575*^9}, {3.965030080886397*^9, 
   3.9650300952946444`*^9}, {3.965030150280223*^9, 3.9650301782466087`*^9}, {
   3.9650311664045477`*^9, 3.965031273549402*^9}, {3.96503232619238*^9, 
   3.965032345438122*^9}, 3.9835590476641912`*^9, 3.991403637840014*^9},
 Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0],
 CellLabel->"In[25]:=",ExpressionUUID->"64e7fd47-7f4b-4c18-9d9a-f37287581017"],

Cell["In this alternative version we do the fit differently . ", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9659535603874807`*^9, 3.96595356852524*^9}, {
   3.965953644494245*^9, 3.965953654278295*^9}, 
   3.966020855867337*^9},ExpressionUUID->"354b6777-7919-4297-973d-\
c0698220137f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "LIke the previous, this code returns two parameters, \[Eta] and \[Theta] .  \
From these, one calculates c as  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["\[Eta]", "\[Mu]"], "+", "\[Theta]"}]], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "29430683-a000-4c6e-920b-7839138d7f3d"],
 " , where \[Mu] is the mean expression level for the gene of interest.\n\n\
Like the previous, the inputs are a matpac, and a number, \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]samplegoal\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], which instructs \
the code to take a random sample of genes, rather than use every gene in the \
matpac.  In practice, using this code, it seems like a sample of 1000-2000 is \
adequate, but of course one can go as high as one likes.  The code divides \
the genes into bins, where the width of a bin corresponds to 1/2 of a log of \
gene expression change, i.e. each bin covers a fold increase in expression of \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SqrtBox["\[ExponentialE]"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "024597e6-8370-47c5-b46d-35a5419adc1d"],
 " = 1.64872.  Then it attempts to sample an equal number from each bin, \
unless there aren\[CloseCurlyQuote]t enough in a bin, in which case it \
samples all of the bin.  As a result, even if the samplegoal =1000, the total \
number sampled may be less than 1000.  The reason for not just sticking to a \
high samplegoal in all cases is that the time required for calculation doesn\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t just depend on the number of genes, it also depends on \
the number of cells, and it slows down a lot if cell number is high.  So \
having the adjustable samplegoal allows one to adjust for that.  \n\nUnlike \
the previous code, this code begins by fitting \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]j\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] which is shorthand for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["c", "2"], ".", "  "}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "e9a2e047-33b1-4532-adee-a7ed9db3b919"],
 "Then it generates data points consisting of pairs {\[Mu], ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "+", "j"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "61850cb8-65d1-496a-8be8-55ae7a5abe97"],
 " \[Mu]}.  In the event that 1+j \[Mu] ends up being below zero, which can \
occasionally happen, the subsequent application of Log to the data points \
will produce imaginary numbers, which will mess up the use of Fitting \
algorithms.  Accordingly, after generating the data points, we remove away \
any that have a negative value for the second element.  \nFinally we fit the \
Logged data to equation \ny== Log[1+\[Eta] +\[Theta] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[ExponentialE]", "x"], "]"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "b26c8b20-ace4-4c47-bca2-0d24f5759bac"],
 ", where y is the Log of the ordinate data value, and x is the Log of the \
corresponding abscissa value.  \n\nThe code prints a graph showing the \
quality of the fit, and then returns the parameters as rules that can be fed \
into BigSur"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.966019897962973*^9, 3.966020037884163*^9}, {
  3.966020078417264*^9, 3.9660201163269176`*^9}, {3.966020203388637*^9, 
  3.966020228969235*^9}, {3.966020374776598*^9, 3.966020675236497*^9}, {
