  3.967158819720984*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f5421543-95b1-4286-a455-\
190d7c7cd4ec"],

Cell["\<\
 Here the syntax for FindZAlt is that it operates on the entire parameters \
list, not just one at a time.  so we write FindZAlt[paramslist] rather than \
FindZAlt/@params.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9671573213437567`*^9, 3.967157424573957*^9}, 
   3.9671574900850763`*^9, {3.967158488866455*^9, 3.9671585028988743`*^9}, {
   3.967158566522663*^9, 3.967158592881036*^9}, {3.967374421783601*^9, 
   3.967374437044539*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"480442f0-068d-4c2f-8066-\
4dccbb78ff45"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FindZAlt", "[", "paramslist_", "]"}], ":=", 
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"TakeSmallestBy", "[", 
      RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "Abs", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "&"}], "/@", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x", "/.", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"ToRules", "[", "#", "]"}], "}"}]}], "&"}], "/@", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"NRoots", "[", 
           RowBox[{"#", ",", "x"}], "]"}], "&"}], "/@", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"0", "==", 
              RowBox[{"#", ".", 
               RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", 
                 RowBox[{"2", " ", "x"}], ",", 
                 RowBox[{"3", " ", 
                  SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}], ",", 
                 RowBox[{"4", " ", 
                  SuperscriptBox["x", "3"]}], ",", "0"}], "}"}]}]}], ")"}], 
            "&"}], "/@", "paramslist"}], ")"}]}], ")"}]}], "/.", 
      RowBox[{"_Complex", "->", " ", "Nothing"}]}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9671572188821507`*^9, 3.967157231969242*^9}, {
   3.967157290301446*^9, 3.967157294170928*^9}, 3.96715748464892*^9, {
   3.9671584610350657`*^9, 3.967158484730074*^9}},
 Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0],
 CellLabel->"In[73]:=",ExpressionUUID->"91cf3149-d3be-4af4-b3e0-f661d5035104"],

Cell["\<\
The equation below finds positions in paramslist where the second derivative \
is zero.  \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967467995841762*^9, 
  3.9674680123491583`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"32706f8b-d23a-4f5f-a666-\
c917f0509071"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FindW", "[", "paramslist_", "]"}], ":=", "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Position", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"x", "/.", 
          RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"#", ".", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"6", "x"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"12", 
                 SuperscriptBox["x", "2"]}], ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "==", "0"}],
             ",", "x"}], "]"}]}], "&"}], "/@", "paramslist"}], ")"}], "/.", 
      RowBox[{"_Complex", "->", " ", "Nothing"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"x_", "/;", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Length", "[", "x", "]"}], ">", "0"}]}]}], "]"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.967467630916175*^9, 3.9674676662540007`*^9}, {
  3.967467716657789*^9, 3.967467722689334*^9}, {3.96746797710608*^9, 
  3.967467981697123*^9}},
 Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0],
 CellLabel->"In[74]:=",ExpressionUUID->"394db4e9-9604-4735-b8bf-feb9abf3a5aa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here are the steps.\n\nWe begin with a list of augmented parameters of \
length Binomial[m,2].  Let use define -X and X as the X-positions \
corresponding to our p-value cutoff.  \n\nStep 1:  We apply QuickTest6CF to \
all the augmented parameters to generate a list of positions called \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 StyleBox["posns1",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] where QuickTest6CF returns 1.  The indexing of \
posns1 runs from 1 to Binomial[m,2].   QuickTest6CF is a fast function that \
takes as input a list of augmented parameters, and a -logpvalue cutoff, and \
outputs 1 or 0 to indicate whether the values of the polynomial at x= -X and \
x=X are different, or whether the values at x= -X and x= X have the same \
sign, but one that is different from the value at x=0.   If they do then, by \
continuity we know that there is a root between -X and X, i.e. a root that \
will produce a -logp-value below the cutoff.   So our first step is to \
identify all the polynomials that cannot be excluded on these grounds.  \n\n\
Step 2:  We know that gene pair correlations involving very lowly expressed \
genes sometimes don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t display an actual root between -X and \
X, but come close to doing so, and should be excluded from further \
consideration whenever that happens.  We call that having a \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]quasiroot\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].   Empirically, we \
find that this happens when the maximum gene expression in the pair is <0.05 \
(given 1662 cells), i.e. when the total UMI in the most highly expressed gene \
amounts to less than 84.  So we need to find the positions in our augmented \
parameters list where there is a quasiroot.  \n\nFirst we generate a Sparse \
Matrix of just gene pairs where the maximum gene expression meets that \
criterion, and then use ListIndex to convert the Explicit Positions to list \
indices.  We then use that to divide the positions from the previous step \
into two groups, \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 StyleBox["posns1high",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
 StyleBox["posns1low",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] for gene expression.  We then take the ",
 StyleBox["posns1low",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and apply SecondTestCF.  This test does a series of things:\n\t1) If the \
slope at -X isn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t positive, there isn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t a \
quasiroot (we find empirically that the slope at -X is always positive, but \
we check anyway)\n\t2) Then, if the slope at X is negative it guarantees a \
maximum between -X and X, which we take to be a quasiroot,\n\t3) If either of \
the only possible inflection points (the positions of which can be solved for \
analytically as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "d"}], "-", 
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"9", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["d", "2"]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{"24", " ", "c", " ", "e"}]}]]}], 
   RowBox[{"12", " ", "e"}]]],
  CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJwdxV0oAwEAB/CLULOXdS9CJ1by8UCUF5tL7U1J0mprJF81ZXtZSRZ1rURt
ykfT0nnhmtiaM8V4WNqyB3aXpSzeeNiDzuaBdWvL/e/h1691xjk+X0UQRIMC
jxacjt/y13AXy6lLm+seTNHH6hU2to15WvLjtg/rEX7XRk6wt5EM4U9SCOOa
qSKPRa3lEq++7d7hoOCO4/NZJoFtrskkdhNbIu6+oF7xVT9VwQzLVP8pW5si
dThARjU49fyow/emJIlt9e0tOP1Ed2LWb+nBvQbvANYclgxY7AuYcEweGsHX
+vQ07gieLmB+MLOEx8pxF67V7a3guVRuDTv0dh82vnwnsDkcesA72WgGH2SF
HJ7wbEh4cV9Wl/OcvajcvFxQZ8y+G/zDnd3ifxWK/Rc=
   "],
  Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0],ExpressionUUID->
  "cd65c6a1-9351-4672-8173-7fd669491df3"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "d"}], "+", 
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"9", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["d", "2"]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{"24", " ", "c", " ", "e"}]}]]}], 
   RowBox[{"12", " ", "e"}]]],
  CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJwdxV0oAwEAB/CLULOXdS9CJ1by8UCUF5tL7U1J0mprJF81ZXtZSRZ1rURt
ykfT0nnhmtiaM8V4WNqyB3aXpSzeeNiDzuaBdWvL/e/h1691xjk+X0UQRIMC
jxacjt/y13AXy6lLm+seTNHH6hU2to15WvLjtg/rEX7XRk6wt5EM4U9SCOOa
qSKPRa3lEq++7d7hoOCO4/NZJoFtrskkdhNbIu6+oF7xVT9VwQzLVP8pW5si
dThARjU49fyow/emJIlt9e0tOP1Ed2LWb+nBvQbvANYclgxY7AuYcEweGsHX
+vQ07gieLmB+MLOEx8pxF67V7a3guVRuDTv0dh82vnwnsDkcesA72WgGH2SF
HJ7wbEh4cV9Wl/OcvajcvFxQZ8y+G/zDnd3ifxWK/Rc=
   "],
  Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0],ExpressionUUID->
  "583c5c72-63e9-4af4-a616-75cece021b23"],
 " ) lies between -X and X, if the slope at either of them is negative then \
there must have been a maximum between -X and X.  Note that the slopes at \
each of these points are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"45", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["d", "3"]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"36", " ", "c", " ", "d", " ", "e"}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"15", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["d", "2"], " ", 
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"9", " ", 
        SuperscriptBox["d", "2"]}], "-", 
       RowBox[{"24", " ", "c", " ", "e"}]}]]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"8", " ", "e", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"9", " ", "b", " ", "e"}], "-", 
       RowBox[{"c", " ", 
        SqrtBox[
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"9", " ", 
           SuperscriptBox["d", "2"]}], "-", 
          RowBox[{"24", " ", "c", " ", "e"}]}]]}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
   RowBox[{"72", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["e", "2"]}]]],
