 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"45", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["d", "3"]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"36", " ", "c", " ", "d", " ", "e"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"15", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["d", "2"], " ", 
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"9", " ", 
        SuperscriptBox["d", "2"]}], "-", 
       RowBox[{"24", " ", "c", " ", "e"}]}]]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{"8", " ", "e", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"9", " ", "b", " ", "e"}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"c", " ", 
        SqrtBox[
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"9", " ", 
           SuperscriptBox["d", "2"]}], "-", 
          RowBox[{"24", " ", "c", " ", "e"}]}]]}]}], ")"}]}]}], 
   RowBox[{"72", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["e", "2"]}]]],
  CellChangeTimes->CompressedData["
1:eJwdxV0oAwEAB/CLULOXdS9CJ1by8UCUF5tL7U1J0mprJF81ZXtZSRZ1rURt
ykfT0nnhmtiaM8V4WNqyB3aXpSzeeNiDzuaBdWvL/e/h1691xjk+X0UQRIMC
jxacjt/y13AXy6lLm+seTNHH6hU2to15WvLjtg/rEX7XRk6wt5EM4U9SCOOa
qSKPRa3lEq++7d7hoOCO4/NZJoFtrskkdhNbIu6+oF7xVT9VwQzLVP8pW5si
dThARjU49fyow/emJIlt9e0tOP1Ed2LWb+nBvQbvANYclgxY7AuYcEweGsHX
+vQ07gieLmB+MLOEx8pxF67V7a3guVRuDTv0dh82vnwnsDkcesA72WgGH2SF
HJ7wbEh4cV9Wl/OcvajcvFxQZ8y+G/zDnd3ifxWK/Rc=
   "],
  Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0],ExpressionUUID->
  "ffff609c-f58f-44af-ac4f-6e0db46c68ae"],
 ", however in testing their signs we may exclude the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"72", 
    SuperscriptBox["e", "2"]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cadf9da2-1938-46ff-94dc-36adac68d8a5"],
 " in the denominator because, being a square it is necessarily positive so \
it has no influence on the sign.  \n\t\nStep 3:  We define ",
 StyleBox["posns2",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " as the union of ",
 StyleBox["posns1high",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " and those elements of ",
 StyleBox["posns1low",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " that passed the slope and intercept tests.  The indexing of these still \
runs from 1 to Binomial[m,2]\n\nStep 4:  We apply Foundroots to \
augmentedParameters[[posns2]].  This finds roots except where no true roots \
exist in which case it returns z.  \n\tTo those cases where no root was  \
found, we use FindZ to return a quasi-root.  We then replace the z\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s with these quasiroots; the whole thing together is called \
",
 StyleBox["rootsComplete",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ".  This list has the same length as posns2.  Thus if we want to find out \
which augmented parameters go with which roots we match them up with \
augmentedparameters[[posns2]].\n\t\nStep 5:  We use Benjamini Hochberg to \
find the significance cutoff for FixedPValFunc/@rootsComplete, using \
Binomial[m,2] as our Array length.   We define ",
 StyleBox["checkposns",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " as those locations within rootsComplete where the BH cutoff was exceeded.  \
In order to get this indexing back to that of augmentedparameters we take ",
 StyleBox["posns2[[checkposns]]",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 "\nStep7:  We now want to search for additional quasiroots, at those \
check-positions, where the quasiroot falls below the BH cutoff.  We remove \
any of those as well from the list.  Finally, we index the list by \
augmentedparameters[[posns2]]"
}], "Text",
